  "anomaly_detected": false,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "The drawing is a faithful build of the spec with permuted reference designators (e.g. the bus connectors are J5/J8, the SS54 is D2, the PMEG3030EP is D3, the IRLML6402 is Q3, the BC857 is Q1, the MAX3485 is U2, the SPDT is SW2). Every component value and type matches the spec exactly: resistors {10k, 5.1k, 47k, 20k, 2k, 2.2k, 2.2k, 1k, 1k, and six 0-ohm jumpers}, capacitors {four 100 uF on the servo rail plus one 0.1 uF on the MAX3485 VCC}, the two Schottky diodes in the correct series orientation (D2 anode at the 5V_POWER jack, D3 anode at +5V feeding the servo rail), the P-FET battery high-side switch with its 47k gate pull-up and SPDT-to-GND, and the BC857 self-switching DE//RE tie on the MAX3485. The only irregularity is a duplicated 'C6' label on two of the four 100 uF caps, which is an annotation/designator collision that does not change the electrical behaviour, so it is not reported as an anomaly."
}

